{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '35,62p' src/cljc/dao/datom.cljc; nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md | sed -n '379,402p;403,424p'; sed -n '188,224p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc; sed -n '365,390p' src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc; date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT'; date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z'\"","aggregated_output":"   coordinates in a slot the spec declares a stream-local gauge, and would put\n   the floor above what an int8-wide e can represent at all.\n\n   See docs/design/datom.md, Reserved Entities.\"\n  16)\n\n\n(defn local-datom?\n  \"True for the runtime-enforced portion of a persisted local d5 datom:\n   `[e a v t m]`, with non-negative integer stream-local coordinates `e` and\n   `t`, integer `m`, and a namespaced keyword attribute. Negative tempids are\n   compilation values and must be resolved before commitment. Canonical value\n   encoding is a separate persistence concern and is not decided here.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (vector? x)\n       (= 5 (count x))\n       (integer? (nth x 0))\n       (not (neg? (nth x 0)))\n       (keyword? (nth x 1))\n       (some? (namespace (nth x 1)))\n       (integer? (nth x 3))\n       (not (neg? (nth x 3)))\n       (integer? (nth x 4))))\n\n\n(defn op\n  \"The m (metadata/op) slot of a datom (a [e a v t m] vector or a Datom record).\"\n  [datom]\n   379\t    the local store.\n   380\t- **Kinds do not mix (D3).** `load` of an address already recorded under\n   381\t  another kind is refused, `:dao.space.dht/kind-conflict`, instead of\n   382\t  silently left. If the candidate's manifest is already recorded by\n   383\t  hand under the index kind, the follower starts nothing, owns nothing,\n   384\t  and reads that record. It never abandons a record that is not of the\n   385\t  candidate kind, and it forgets one in a single case, the Unloadable\n   386\t  rule below: a `:failed` index-kind record at its candidate's address.\n   387\t  That record is the user's throughout: once `:loaded` it is in the\n   388\t  snapshot set as any index load made by hand is, whatever the\n   389\t  follower's verdict on the trace, and no release removes it. A record\n   390\t  of any other kind at the candidate's address is neither read,\n   391\t  forgotten nor restarted: the candidate is reported\n   392\t  `:yin.head/unloadable` once with that record's failure and waits\n   393\t  until the record's owner removes it, and then loads as a candidate.\n   394\t  A `load-index` by hand of a manifest that is loading\n   395\t  as a candidate is refused with that code as data (H1 carries the\n   396\t  host module's translation), and succeeds once the head is installed.\n   397\t- **`abandon` leaves nothing behind.**\n   398\t  `(dao.space.dht/abandon node address)` removes a `:loading` record,\n   399\t  emits no event, and retires that record's interest in the fetch\n   400\t  client: the retained unsent request, if it is this record's, by\n   401\t  `dao.jing.content.step/abandon`; otherwise its outstanding id by\n   402\t  `dao.jing.content.step/retire`, after which a late answer is\n   403\t  unsolicited and dropped. Both functions exist. Each load has its own\n   404\t  request id, so another load fetching the same address is untouched.\n   405\t  `advance-loads` today steps the client only while a record is\n   406\t  `:loading` (`dao/space/dht.cljc:1313-1321`); it changes to step it\n   407\t  whenever a record is loading **or the client holds an unsent request,\n   408\t  an outstanding id or an undelivered completion**, so what an abandon\n   409\t  leaves is drained with no load active. What remains outside the node\n   410\t  is one get inside the DHT, which ends by the DHT's own `get-ticks`\n   411\t  and whose answer nobody claims.\n   412\t- **Confirmed.** The load is `:loaded` and the greatest `t` of its\n   413\t  datoms equals the sequence. The follower emits `:confirmed` with the\n   414\t  trace and changes nothing else (5.7).\n   415\t- **Rejected.** The load is `:loaded` and the check fails:\n   416\t  `:yin.head/seq-mismatch`. The candidate is dropped, its address\n   417\t  released, and its envelope id kept as the principal's **last\n   418\t  rejected**, one value, so the same trace shown at every poll is not\n   419\t  loaded again. The floor is where it was. Any other candidate trace\n   420\t  takes the slot as usual. One value remembers one trace: two wrong\n   421\t  traces shown in alternation are each walked again each time. After\n   422\t  the first time their blobs are local, so that is a local walk, not a\n   423\t  fetch.\n   424\t- **What one slot does not give: progress under replay.** Every signed\n  \"The authority events of every snapshot, assembled per snapshot (an\n   entity id is local to its index) and concatenated in snapshot order,\n   each envelope with its proof once.\"\n  [node snapshot]\n  (into []\n        (comp (mapcat (fn [s]\n                        (authority/events-from-datoms\n                          (filter (fn [[_ a]]\n                                    (contains? #{:yin.module/envelope\n                                                 :yin.module/proof}\n                                               a))\n                                  (snapshot-datoms node s)))))\n              (distinct))\n        snapshot))\n\n\n(defn authority\n  \"The reader's authority from its composition (7.1): each declared\n   public key (64 lowercase hex) a principal whose proof is an Ed25519\n   signature (6.3), at `:seq-floor` 0, and `name-env`'s direct entries.\"\n  [{:keys [principals name-env]}]\n  {:principals (into {}\n                     (map (fn [public]\n                            [(sign/principal public)\n                             {:proof :yin.module/signature\n                              :key public\n                              :verify sign/verify-envelope\n                              :seq-floor 0}]))\n                     principals)\n   :name-env (or name-env {})})\n\n\n(defn- fold\n  \"The fold of the reader's snapshot set under `authority`\n   `{:principals {principal declaration} :name-env {name address}}`, and\n   every envelope it saw by id.  A retraction whose target is not an\n   assertion the snapshot set holds -- none, or another retraction --\n\n\n(defn- decode-plain-completion\n  \"Total decode of one completion no materialization claims: the answer\n   conforms to its request's vocabulary or the completion carries an\n   :error; a loss carries :lost.\"\n  [completion]\n  (let [{:keys [id request lost answer]} completion]\n    (cond\n      lost {:id id, :lost lost}\n\n      (contains? request get-op)\n      (cond\n        (not (get-answer? answer)) {:id id, :error malformed-response}\n        (not (get answer :jing/found?))\n        {:id id, :found? false, :value nil}\n        :else\n        (let [value (accepted-value (get request get-op)\n                                    (get answer :jing/bytes))]\n          (if (identical? refused value)\n            {:id id, :error integrity-failure}\n            {:id id, :found? true, :value value})))\n\n      (unacknowledged-answer? answer)\n      {:id id, :error (unacknowledged answer)}\n\n2026-10-05 16:45:14 GMT\n2026-10-05 23:45:14 +07\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
